  <ym-title|Collision-pole separation and the circulation null
  test><label|collision-pole-separation-and-the-circulation-null-test>

  Status: author draft; independent mathematical/source review pending.
  Source pin: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/free-collision-pole-separation.tex>.
  Labels: <verbatim|sec:free-collision-pole-separation>,
  <verbatim|lem:collision-radial-separation>,
  <verbatim|lem:collision-product-separation>,
  <verbatim|thm:free-circulation-null>. Author: parent
  hairer-codex-existence-20261111. This disjoint unit was split from the Luna
  classifier after independent review identified a missing
  harmonic/product-pole separation. The classifier author retains generic
  probe/determinant elimination, quiet-charge classification and finite
  scenes.

  <section|Exact source map><label|exact-source-map>

  All names below lie in <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free> unless qualified
  otherwise.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|rad>, <verbatim|Clears>, <verbatim|Pole>,
    <verbatim|green_pole>, <verbatim|Pole.step>, <verbatim|Pole.taylor>,
    <verbatim|kernel_pole>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/Pole.lean>: degree
    <verbatim|-r>, harmonicity, and globally smooth radial numerator after
    multiplying by <verbatim|\|z\|^(2(r-1))>. The prose derives the numerator
    differentiation formula and all kernel orders from the canonical
    covariance, rather than treating harmonicity as a new input. It only uses
    smoothness, a consequence of the source's <verbatim|ContDiff ... omega>.

    <item><verbatim|lap_valued>, <verbatim|clears_faint>,
    <verbatim|Faint.lean>: Laplacian coefficient <verbatim|4(s+1)(s+2-r)> in
    four dimensions, clearing descent, and homogeneity plus continuity at
    zero. The zero coefficient at the genuine pole clearing order is not
    divided by; descent only uses exponents strictly below r-1.

    <item><verbatim|Silt>, <verbatim|Echoes>, <verbatim|Deep>,
    <verbatim|Silt.twice>, private <verbatim|sum_peel>,
    <verbatim|Deep.clear>, <verbatim|Silt.lean>: product poles homogeneous of
    degree -q with radial clearing q-2; finite highest-degree peeling
    separates them from a harmonic residue. Prose writes natural truncation
    <verbatim|max(q-2,0)> explicitly. No false plain limit of the full
    colliding moment is asserted.

    <item><verbatim|Rack>, <verbatim|shelf>, <verbatim|Shelves.lean>: jet
    cutoff j, not weighted cap d. <verbatim|eat>, <verbatim|Recurse.lean>;
    <verbatim|singleBite>, <verbatim|all_bite>, <verbatim|upper_shelf>,
    <verbatim|circulate>, <verbatim|circulate_eval>, <verbatim|Morsels.lean>:
    finite coordinate contraction derivation and same-colour quadratic
    circulation. Polynomial derivations do not act on z.

    <item><verbatim|path_wield>, <verbatim|chorus>, <verbatim|Deep.weaker>,
    <verbatim|duet_path>, <verbatim|Frenzy.lean>: continuous distant
    contractions, highest jet residue, lower-order suppression, and exact
    double-hit expansion into product poles. Orders are 4+k+s and 8+k+l+s+b;
    M is strictly greater than 8+k+l+2j.

    <item><verbatim|front_egress>, private <verbatim|cluster_in>,
    <verbatim|vertex>, <verbatim|cluster_clear>, <verbatim|Rumbles.lean>:
    four contraction placements, reconstruction of the surviving single-hit
    sum by the one-leg Wick identity, eventual separated configuration along
    every fixed nonzero direction, and gauge-invariant colour sum. Local
    vanishing uses the original null capacity because the added quadratic
    test has grade k+l+4\<less\>=d. The source requires l\<less\>k; it does
    not impose l\<less\>j here. That latter inequality belongs to the
    separate weighted-degree drop in <verbatim|circulates_lower> and must be
    checked by the classifier consumer.
  </itemize-minus>

  The chapter's top theorem is exactly the same-capacity null conclusion of
  <verbatim|cluster_clear> for P in shelf j. It does not prove the generic
  invertibility of the colour-probe matrix, the uniform external detector, or
  the classification of quiet charges. These remain in the separate
  classifier chapter.

  <section|Inputs and literature><label|inputs-and-literature>

  Reuse the explicit free Maxwell covariance and Wick polynomial convention
  of <verbatim|free-maxwell-ward-flux.tex>; the calculation here expands the
  singularity argument required by the actual classifier. Source-level
  shelves and flavours are interpreted through their definitions, not names.
  Existing shared literature notes were checked in the parent session; no
  exact literature replacement is asserted for this tailored collision lemma.
  The radial calculation, finite asymptotic peeling and Wick contractions are
  all proved explicitly.

  <section|Commands actually run and limits><label|commands-actually-run-and-limits>

  Read Pole.lean in two bounded chunks (1\U145,145\U280), and all of
  Faint.lean, Silt.lean, Frenzy.lean and Rumbles.lean. Read Morsels.lean
  1\U130 including the contraction definitions, Shelves.lean1\U75 and
  Recurse.lean1\U52 for meanings. Used scoped <verbatim|rg> to find
  definitions and existing canonical labels. Two guessed paths
  Probes.lean/Tides.lean did not exist; the actual files above were located.
  No Lean changes, fresh Lean build or axiom replay. LaTeX/visual/structural
  checks and independent review are pending at draft creation.

  Review should check radial powers (squared radius versus radius), Laplacian
  coefficient and nonzero range, the finite product-pole peeling, all four
  Wick placements, no hidden uniform-in-direction limit, and the exact
  jet/grade hypotheses of the final null test.

